  "recommendation": {
    "decision": "VETO",
    "reason": "Both prior exploit classes are otherwise closed: equivalent universal globs and nested .git segments now fail in schema/manual validation, the prefix matcher rejects product and prefix-collision paths, and descriptor-relative O_NOFOLLOW TOCTOU regressions pass. However, _validate_path_pattern checks only the prefix length after stripping /**. It accepts a 513-character pattern rejected by the schema, and that pattern authorizes a valid 512-character descendant. This violates the required schema/manual fail-closed parity.",
    "next_action": "Validate full recursive-pattern length before suffix parsing and add explicit 512/513 boundary regressions, then refreeze."
  },
